stateDiagram-v2
    %% CURRENT implementation; sources and guards in transition inventory.
    state "NOTHING id=0 (reference only)" as NOTHING
    state "IDLE id=10" as IDLE
    state "PENDING id=20" as PENDING
    state "COMPLETED id=30" as COMPLETED
    state "FAILED id=40" as FAILED
    [*] --> IDLE
    IDLE --> PENDING: SignUpTermination terminal retention
    FAILED --> PENDING: SignUpTermination replay / cleanup worker
    PENDING --> COMPLETED: cleanup successful
    PENDING --> FAILED: cleanup exception
    PENDING --> PENDING: cleanup attempt
    COMPLETED --> [*]
    NOTHING --> PENDING: SignUpArtifactCleanup public call
    IDLE --> PENDING: SignUpArtifactCleanup public call
    FAILED --> PENDING: SignUpArtifactCleanup public call
    note right of NOTHING
        NOTHING has no ordinary entry path.
        FAILED is retryable; cap may strand it.
        Public cleanup can be called before enqueue.
    end note
